From cf2f7419c4b07be0cde019abd9edb61eff57a852 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:12:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(libc): convert guest long double at its boundaries

Add GuestLongDouble to load and store the guest's x87 80-bit values,
so the libc can compute with a host long double that is not x87
extended, such as aarch64's binary128, when built for a lifted guest.
Formatting, scanning, strtold, modfl, _LDtest and the code that takes
80-bit values apart go through it; strtold parses with round-to-odd
so that the final rounding is correct. On an x87 host it only copies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015taLuK6Ak1pT1P849L2eqq
